{
	title: 'Commit hook: plugins tell the model about a Bash call commits',
	spec: 'commits.committed(info) (src/host/commits.ts), async, returns lines; by default none. After a Bash call (foreground or background) ends, each commit it made whose Session trailer names the calling session goes to commits.committed, and the lines it returns are appended to that call result after a blank line, so the model and the opened Bash card see them. info: sessionId, callId, cwd, root (repository top level), hash, short, subject, amend, files (absolute path, lines added and removed; a binary file counts -1); hooks may rewrite the counts in place, and the commit card (task 179) shows them as the hooks leave them. Files come from one git show --numstat per such commit and the top level from one git rev-parse, both only when such commits exist; calls without commits cost nothing more. A hook failure goes to diag.log and never fails the Bash result. A commit another concurrent call claims first (task hy announces each hash once) reaches no hook: accepted.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['hy', 'an']
}
